From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:42:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: sequencing: pcie-m2: Copy the connector's BD address
 to the BT node

When a Qualcomm Bluetooth controller reports the default address from
its NVM file, btqca sets HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY and the Bluetooth
core looks for local-bd-address in the firmware node of the serdev
device. For an M.2 card that is the node this driver creates at runtime,
which holds only a compatible. The controller is then registered
unconfigured and cannot be used until user space sets a public address.
The WCN7850 in the Microsoft Surface Laptop 8 behaves this way. The
address assigned to the laptop is known to the system firmware, and the
boot loader can pass it to Linux in the connector node.

If the connector node has a local-bd-address, copy it into the runtime
Bluetooth node.

TODO: Manivannan Sadhasivam's posted rework of M.2 Bluetooth
instantiation onto the auxiliary bus removes the runtime node. With it,
the address has to reach the Bluetooth driver another way.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c
index 291c7410e7c..fbb3713ab9f 100644
--- a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c
+++ b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c
@@ -214,6 +214,7 @@ static int pwrseq_pcie_m2_create_bt_node(struct pwrseq_pcie_m2_ctx *ctx,
 	struct device *dev = ctx->dev;
 	const char *compatible;
 	struct device_node *np;
+	u8 bd_addr[6];
 	int ret;
 
 	id = pci_match_id(pwrseq_m2_pci_ids, pdev);
@@ -241,6 +242,17 @@ static int pwrseq_pcie_m2_create_bt_node(struct pwrseq_pcie_m2_ctx *ctx,
 		goto err_destroy_changeset;
 	}
 
+	/* A BD address provided by the platform firmware for the fitted card */
+	if (!of_property_read_u8_array(ctx->of_node, "local-bd-address", bd_addr,
+				       sizeof(bd_addr))) {
+		ret = of_changeset_add_prop_u8_array(pci_dev->ocs, np, "local-bd-address",
+						     bd_addr, sizeof(bd_addr));
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(dev, "Failed to add bluetooth address: %d\n", ret);
+			goto err_destroy_changeset;
+		}
+	}
+
 	ret = of_changeset_apply(pci_dev->ocs);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "Failed to apply changeset: %d\n", ret);
-- 
